340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Value Clarification Matrix: This tool helps prioritize AI projects by assessing them against multiple criteria: Business Value \(revenue/cost impact\), Environmental Impact \(resource reduction\), Social Impact \(accessibility/inclusion\), Implementation Risk, and Total Cost of Ownership \(lifetime resource needs\). It encourages a holistic view beyond pure technical performance. )
/E (Value Clarification Matrix: This tool helps prioritize AI projects by assessing them against multiple criteria: Business Value \(revenue/cost impact\), Environmental Impact \(resource reduction\), Social Impact \(accessibility/inclusion\), Implementation Risk, and Total Cost of Ownership \(lifetime resource needs\). It encourages a holistic view beyond pure technical performance. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Total Cost of Ownership \(TCO\) & ROI: Frugal AI necessitates moving beyond rudimentary ROI calculations. A comprehensive TCO analysis must include not only initial development costs but also ongoing infrastructure, compute, energy, data storage, and maintenance expenses over the AI system's lifecycle. Accurately measuring TCO and linking it to tangible ROI is vital for demonstrating the economic benefits of frugal approaches. )
/E (Total Cost of Ownership \(TCO\) & ROI: Frugal AI necessitates moving beyond rudimentary ROI calculations. A comprehensive TCO analysis must include not only initial development costs but also ongoing infrastructure, compute, energy, data storage, and maintenance expenses over the AI system's lifecycle. Accurately measuring TCO and linking it to tangible ROI is vital for demonstrating the economic benefits of frugal approaches. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (AI Energy Scoring: This involves measuring and benchmarking the energy consumed by AI models during training and inference relative to their performance \(e.g., accuracy, latency\). Tools like ML CO2 impact calculators and standardized scoring systems help compare models based on their energy efficiency, guiding developers towards more sustainable choices. )
/E (AI Energy Scoring: This involves measuring and benchmarking the energy consumed by AI models during training and inference relative to their performance \(e.g., accuracy, latency\). Tools like ML CO2 impact calculators and standardized scoring systems help compare models based on their energy efficiency, guiding developers towards more sustainable choices. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Standardization \(e.g., AFNOR Spec 2314\): Initiatives like the French AFNOR specification provide concrete benchmarks and guidelines for evaluating the environmental impact of AI services. Such standards encourage transparency and accountability by requiring justification for using AI over less intensive alternatives, adherence to best practices throughout the lifecycle, and consideration of planetary boundaries. Further development and international adoption of such standards are key. )
/E (Standardization \(e.g., AFNOR Spec 2314\): Initiatives like the French AFNOR specification provide concrete benchmarks and guidelines for evaluating the environmental impact of AI services. Such standards encourage transparency and accountability by requiring justification for using AI over less intensive alternatives, adherence to best practices throughout the lifecycle, and consideration of planetary boundaries. Further development and international adoption of such standards are key. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
